#: includes/strings.php:23
msgid "REST User Discovery"
msgstr "REST User Discovery"

#: includes/strings.php:24
msgid "Hide users from anonymous REST requests"
msgstr "Hide users from anonymous REST requests"

#: includes/strings.php:25
msgid ""
"Stops the REST API from listing account login names to logged-out visitors. "
"Without it, anyone can read <code>/wp/v2/users</code> and collect valid "
"usernames — half of what a password-guessing attack needs, so the attacker "
"no longer has to find the username first."
msgstr ""
"Stops the REST API from listing account login names to logged-out visitors. "
"Without it, anyone can read <code>/wp/v2/users</code> and collect valid "
"usernames — half of what a password-guessing attack needs, so the attacker "
"no longer has to find the username first."

#: includes/strings.php:28
msgid "REST Authentication"
msgstr "REST Authentication"

#: includes/strings.php:29
msgid "Require authentication for all REST requests"
msgstr "Require authentication for all REST requests"

#: includes/strings.php:30
msgid ""
"Blocks anonymous REST entirely and stops advertising the endpoint. The "
"logged-in block editor still works, but public blocks, search, and "
"integrations may not. <code>oembed/1.0</code> stays open so other sites can "
"still embed your posts — it serves only what a published post already shows. "
"Filter: <code>keel_public_rest_routes</code>."
msgstr ""
"Blocks anonymous REST entirely and stops advertising the endpoint. The "
"logged-in block editor still works, but public blocks, search, and "
"integrations may not. <code>oembed/1.0</code> stays open so other sites can "
"still embed your posts — it serves only what a published post already shows. "
"Filter: <code>keel_public_rest_routes</code>."

#: includes/strings.php:33
msgid "XML-RPC Pingbacks"
msgstr "XML-RPC Pingbacks"

#: includes/strings.php:34
msgid "Accept incoming pingbacks"
msgstr "Accept incoming pingbacks"

#: includes/strings.php:35
msgid ""
"Off by default. Removes <code>pingback.ping</code> — a spam/reflection-DDoS "
"vector — and the <code>X-Pingback</code> header."
msgstr ""
"Off by default. Removes <code>pingback.ping</code> — a spam/reflection-DDoS "
"vector — and the <code>X-Pingback</code> header."

#: includes/strings.php:38
msgid "XML-RPC Remote Publishing"
msgstr "XML-RPC Remote Publishing"

#: includes/strings.php:39
msgid "Allow remote publishing (blogging apps)"
msgstr "Allow remote publishing (blogging apps)"

#: includes/strings.php:40
msgid ""
"Off by default. Removes credential-authenticated <code>wp.*/metaWeblog/MT/"
"blogger</code> methods and the RSD link. Leave it on while Jetpack is active "
"unless connection and feature testing proves it unnecessary."
msgstr ""
"Off by default. Removes credential-authenticated <code>wp.*/metaWeblog/MT/"
"blogger</code> methods and the RSD link. Leave it on while Jetpack is active "
"unless connection and feature testing proves it unnecessary."

#: includes/strings.php:43
msgid "XML-RPC Multicall"
msgstr "XML-RPC Multicall"

#: includes/strings.php:44
msgid "Allow <code>system.multicall</code>"
msgstr "Allow <code>system.multicall</code>"

#: includes/strings.php:45
msgid ""
"Off by default. <code>system.multicall</code> bundles many XML-RPC calls "
"into one request. WordPress 4.4 prevented it from being abused as a password-"
"guessing multiplier, so refusing it today is minor attack-surface reduction "
"and does not block any live threat. However, almost nothing legitimately "
"uses this method, so leaving it off is safe."
msgstr ""
"Off by default. <code>system.multicall</code> bundles many XML-RPC calls "
"into one request. WordPress 4.4 prevented it from being abused as a password-"
"guessing multiplier, so refusing it today is minor attack-surface reduction "
"and does not block any live threat. However, almost nothing legitimately "
"uses this method, so leaving it off is safe."

#: includes/strings.php:48
msgid "XML-RPC Endpoint"
msgstr "XML-RPC Endpoint"

#: includes/strings.php:49
msgid "Block the endpoint entirely (returns 403)"
msgstr "Block the endpoint entirely (returns 403)"

#: includes/strings.php:50
msgid ""
"Strictest tier — <code>xmlrpc.php</code> answers 403 for every request. "
"Leave XML-RPC reachable while Jetpack is active, unless connection and "
"feature testing proves Jetpack no longer needs it. See the XML-RPC help tab "
"for why this runs inside WordPress and when blocking further out is better."
msgstr ""
"Strictest tier — <code>xmlrpc.php</code> answers 403 for every request. "
"Leave XML-RPC reachable while Jetpack is active, unless connection and "
"feature testing proves Jetpack no longer needs it. See the XML-RPC help tab "
"for why this runs inside WordPress and when blocking further out is better."

#: includes/strings.php:53
msgid "Application Passwords"
msgstr "Application Passwords"

#: includes/strings.php:54
msgid "Prohibit application passwords"
msgstr "Prohibit application passwords"

#: includes/strings.php:55
msgid ""
"Off by default — application passwords are hashed, revocable, per-"
"application credentials for REST and XML-RPC, and usually the safest way to "
"grant API access. They carry the owning account's full access and skip "
"interactive 2FA, so prohibit them only when policy requires every login to "
"pass 2FA or SSO, or when no integration needs API access at all."
msgstr ""
"Off by default — application passwords are hashed, revocable, per-"
"application credentials for REST and XML-RPC, and usually the safest way to "
"grant API access. They carry the owning account's full access and skip "
"interactive 2FA, so prohibit them only when policy requires every login to "
"pass 2FA or SSO, or when no integration needs API access at all."

#: includes/strings.php:59
msgid "Require strong passwords"
msgstr "Require strong passwords"

#: includes/strings.php:60
msgid ""
"15+ characters, not your username or email name, not a common choice, and "
"not found in a known breach. Every account is breach-screened, including the "
"roles exempted below — the exemption covers the other rules only. See the "
"Help tab for why the rules are shaped this way and what the breach check "
"sends."
msgstr ""
"15+ characters, not your username or email name, not a common choice, and "
"not found in a known breach. Every account is breach-screened, including the "
"roles exempted below — the exemption covers the other rules only. See the "
"Help tab for why the rules are shaped this way and what the breach check "
"sends."

#: includes/strings.php:63
msgid "Password Policy Exemptions"
msgstr "Password Policy Exemptions"

#: includes/strings.php:64
msgid ""
"Roles that skip the length, common-password and username rules; breach "
"screening still applies to everyone. Only roles with no content or settings "
"capabilities appear — which is why Contributor does not. A user is exempt "
"only if every role they hold is listed here. Filter: <code>keel_weak_roles</"
"code>."
msgstr ""
"Roles that skip the length, common-password and username rules; breach "
"screening still applies to everyone. Only roles with no content or settings "
"capabilities appear — which is why Contributor does not. A user is exempt "
"only if every role they hold is listed here. Filter: <code>keel_weak_roles</"
"code>."

#: includes/strings.php:67
msgid "Unfiltered HTML"
msgstr "Unfiltered HTML"

#: includes/strings.php:68
msgid "Limit raw HTML and JavaScript to Administrators"
msgstr "Limit raw HTML and JavaScript to Administrators"

#: includes/strings.php:69
msgid ""
"Removes the <code>unfiltered_html</code> capability from Editors and every "
"non-Administrator, so only Administrators (and Super Admins on multisite) "
"can save raw, unfiltered HTML and scripts. Cuts stored-XSS risk from lower-"
"privileged editorial accounts. On by default."
msgstr ""
"Removes the <code>unfiltered_html</code> capability from Editors and every "
"non-Administrator, so only Administrators (and Super Admins on multisite) "
"can save raw, unfiltered HTML and scripts. Cuts stored-XSS risk from lower-"
"privileged editorial accounts. On by default."

#: includes/strings.php:72
msgid "Version Fingerprint"
msgstr "Version Fingerprint"

#: includes/strings.php:73
msgid "Remove the WordPress version fingerprint"
msgstr "Remove the WordPress version fingerprint"

#: includes/strings.php:74
msgid ""
"Strips the generator meta tag. Obscurity, not hardening — it trims scanner "
"noise but does not make an out-of-date site any safer, and the version still "
"leaks from asset query strings and feeds."
msgstr ""
"Strips the generator meta tag. Obscurity, not hardening — it trims scanner "
"noise but does not make an out-of-date site any safer, and the version still "
"leaks from asset query strings and feeds."

#: includes/strings.php:77
msgid "Security Headers"
msgstr "Security Headers"

#: includes/strings.php:78
msgid "Send baseline security headers"
msgstr "Send baseline security headers"

#: includes/strings.php:79
msgid ""
"<code>X-Content-Type-Options</code>: <code>nosniff</code> and <code>Referrer-"
"Policy</code>: <code>strict-origin-when-cross-origin</code>. Both are low-"
"risk. Framing is controlled separately below, because that is the one that "
"can break a site. Already-set headers are never overwritten."
msgstr ""
"<code>X-Content-Type-Options</code>: <code>nosniff</code> and <code>Referrer-"
"Policy</code>: <code>strict-origin-when-cross-origin</code>. Both are low-"
"risk. Framing is controlled separately below, because that is the one that "
"can break a site. Already-set headers are never overwritten."

#: includes/strings.php:82
msgid "Frame Options"
msgstr "Frame Options"

#: includes/strings.php:83
msgid ""
"Controls who may embed this site in an iframe. <code>SAMEORIGIN</code> "
"blocks cross-origin framing, which stops clickjacking but also breaks "
"legitimate embeds — a client intranet, a partner site, or a preview/proofing "
"tool — usually as a silent blank frame. Leave unchanged if your host or CDN "
"already sets this header, or if the site is meant to be embedded elsewhere."
msgstr ""
"Controls who may embed this site in an iframe. <code>SAMEORIGIN</code> "
"blocks cross-origin framing, which stops clickjacking but also breaks "
"legitimate embeds — a client intranet, a partner site, or a preview/proofing "
"tool — usually as a silent blank frame. Leave unchanged if your host or CDN "
"already sets this header, or if the site is meant to be embedded elsewhere."

#: includes/strings.php:85
msgid "SAMEORIGIN — only this site may frame it"
msgstr "SAMEORIGIN — only this site may frame it"

#: includes/strings.php:86
msgid "DENY — nobody may frame it"
msgstr "DENY — nobody may frame it"

#: includes/strings.php:87
msgid "Leave unchanged (host/CDN sets it, or the site is embedded elsewhere)"
msgstr "Leave unchanged (host/CDN sets it, or the site is embedded elsewhere)"

#: includes/strings.php:91
msgid "AI Connectors"
msgstr "AI Connectors"

#: includes/strings.php:92
msgid "Disable AI provider connectors"
msgstr "Disable AI provider connectors"

#: includes/strings.php:93
msgid ""
"Turns off WordPress 7.0 AI provider connectors via the <code>wp_supports_ai</"
"code> gate and closes the core Connectors screen. Also fires "
"<code>keel_disable_ai_connectors</code> for AI integrations core does not "
"know about."
msgstr ""
"Turns off WordPress 7.0 AI provider connectors via the <code>wp_supports_ai</"
"code> gate and closes the core Connectors screen. Also fires "
"<code>keel_disable_ai_connectors</code> for AI integrations core does not "
"know about."

#: includes/strings.php:96
msgid "Core Auto-Updates"
msgstr "Core Auto-Updates"

#: includes/strings.php:97
msgid ""
"Chooses which core updates install automatically. Minor releases are "
"maintenance and security fixes; major releases are feature updates that can "
"break incompatible themes and plugins. If an explicit <code>wp-config.php</"
"code> policy exists, it takes precedence, and then this control is locked."
msgstr ""
"Chooses which core updates install automatically. Minor releases are "
"maintenance and security fixes; major releases are feature updates that can "
"break incompatible themes and plugins. If an explicit <code>wp-config.php</"
"code> policy exists, it takes precedence, and then this control is locked."

#: includes/strings.php:99
msgid "Maintenance/security releases only — recommended"
msgstr "Maintenance/security releases only — recommended"

#: includes/strings.php:100
msgid "All stable releases"
msgstr "All stable releases"

#: includes/strings.php:101
msgid "No automatic core releases"
msgstr "No automatic core releases"

#: includes/strings.php:102
msgid "Leave unchanged (WordPress, host, or another plugin decides)"
msgstr "Leave unchanged (WordPress, host, or another plugin decides)"

#: includes/strings.php:106
msgid "Translations"
msgstr "Translations"

#: includes/strings.php:107
msgid "Automatically update translation files"
msgstr "Automatically update translation files"

#: includes/strings.php:108
msgid ""
"Installs available WordPress, plugin, and theme language updates. Plugin and "
"theme code updates remain controlled by WordPress's individual per-item "
"choices."
msgstr ""
"Installs available WordPress, plugin, and theme language updates. Plugin and "
"theme code updates remain controlled by WordPress's individual per-item "
"choices."

#: includes/strings.php:111
msgid "Comments"
msgstr "Comments"

#: includes/strings.php:112
msgid "Disable comments, trackbacks, and pingbacks"
msgstr "Disable comments, trackbacks, and pingbacks"

#: includes/strings.php:113
msgid ""
"Closes comments everywhere, hides existing threads, defaults new content to "
"closed, and reports a count of zero. Removes the admin menu, admin-bar node, "
"Recent Comments dashboard widget, comment feeds, and the comment blocks — "
"both from the inserter and from what a block theme renders. Nothing is "
"deleted: turn this off and every comment comes back."
msgstr ""
"Closes comments everywhere, hides existing threads, defaults new content to "
"closed, and reports a count of zero. Removes the admin menu, admin-bar node, "
"Recent Comments dashboard widget, comment feeds, and the comment blocks — "
"both from the inserter and from what a block theme renders. Nothing is "
"deleted: turn this off and every comment comes back."

#: includes/strings.php:116
msgid "Pingbacks On New Posts"
msgstr "Pingbacks On New Posts"

#: includes/strings.php:117
msgid "Close pingbacks and trackbacks on new posts by default"
msgstr "Close pingbacks and trackbacks on new posts by default"

#: includes/strings.php:118
msgid "Sets the \"allow pingbacks\" default to off for newly created content."
msgstr "Sets the \"allow pingbacks\" default to off for newly created content."

#: includes/strings.php:121
msgid "Self-Pingbacks"
msgstr "Self-Pingbacks"

#: includes/strings.php:122
msgid "Disable self-pingbacks"
msgstr "Disable self-pingbacks"

#: includes/strings.php:123
msgid "Stops internal links from generating pingback noise."
msgstr "Stops internal links from generating pingback noise."

#: includes/strings.php:126
msgid "Author Archives"
msgstr "Author Archives"

#: includes/strings.php:127
msgid "Disable public author archives"
msgstr "Disable public author archives"

#: includes/strings.php:128
msgid ""
"Redirects the HTML <code>/author/{slug}/</code> archive to the home page and "
"returns 404 for its feed. Author pages leak usernames (like the REST list "
"above) and are usually thin, duplicate content."
msgstr ""
"Redirects the HTML <code>/author/{slug}/</code> archive to the home page and "
"returns 404 for its feed. Author pages leak usernames (like the REST list "
"above) and are usually thin, duplicate content."

#: includes/strings.php:131
msgid "Attachment Pages"
msgstr "Attachment Pages"

#: includes/strings.php:132
msgid "Redirect attachment pages to the parent post"
msgstr "Redirect attachment pages to the parent post"

#: includes/strings.php:133
msgid ""
"Sends thin attachment pages to the parent post, or to the file itself when "
"the media is unattached. Skipped automatically when the theme provides "
"<code>attachment.php</code> or <code>image.php</code>, since the theme means "
"to render them. Core has its own switch since 6.4 "
"(<code>wp_attachment_pages_enabled</code>); this prefers the parent post "
"over the bare file."
msgstr ""
"Sends thin attachment pages to the parent post, or to the file itself when "
"the media is unattached. Skipped automatically when the theme provides "
"<code>attachment.php</code> or <code>image.php</code>, since the theme means "
"to render them. Core has its own switch since 6.4 "
"(<code>wp_attachment_pages_enabled</code>); this prefers the parent post "
"over the bare file."

#: includes/strings.php:136
msgid "Emoji Script"
msgstr "Emoji Script"

#: includes/strings.php:137
msgid "Disable the emoji detection script"
msgstr "Disable the emoji detection script"

#: includes/strings.php:138
msgid "Removes the emoji detection script and inline CSS from every page."
msgstr "Removes the emoji detection script and inline CSS from every page."

#: includes/strings.php:141
msgid "Post Passwords"
msgstr "Post Passwords"

#: includes/strings.php:142
msgid "Hide post password protection in the editor"
msgstr "Hide post password protection in the editor"

#: includes/strings.php:143
msgid ""
"Hides the \"Password protected\" visibility option in the editor. WordPress "
"post passwords are weak and are bypassed by full-page caching, which serves "
"the same cached page regardless. Existing password-protected posts keep "
"their field so they stay editable. Off by default."
msgstr ""
"Hides the \"Password protected\" visibility option in the editor. WordPress "
"post passwords are weak and are bypassed by full-page caching, which serves "
"the same cached page regardless. Existing password-protected posts keep "
"their field so they stay editable. Off by default."

#: includes/strings.php:146
msgid "Post Revision Retention"
msgstr "Post Revision Retention"

#: includes/strings.php:147
msgid "revisions"
msgstr "revisions"

#: includes/strings.php:148
msgid "revision"
msgstr "revision"

#: includes/strings.php:150
msgid "Unlimited"
msgstr "Unlimited"

#: includes/strings.php:151
msgid "Disabled"
msgstr "Disabled"

#: includes/strings.php:153
msgid ""
"Maximum revisions WordPress keeps for each post. Enter <code>-1</code> for "
"unlimited or <code>0</code> to disable revisions. Changing this governs "
"future saves; it does not immediately delete revisions already stored. A "
"numeric or false <code>WP_POST_REVISIONS</code> value in <code>wp-"
"config.php</code> takes precedence."
msgstr ""
"Maximum revisions WordPress keeps for each post. Enter <code>-1</code> for "
"unlimited or <code>0</code> to disable revisions. Changing this governs "
"future saves; it does not immediately delete revisions already stored. A "
"numeric or false <code>WP_POST_REVISIONS</code> value in <code>wp-"
"config.php</code> takes precedence."

#: includes/strings.php:156
msgid "Classic Editor"
msgstr "Classic Editor"

#: includes/strings.php:157
msgid "Use the Classic editor instead of the block editor"
msgstr "Use the Classic editor instead of the block editor"

#: includes/strings.php:158
msgid ""
"Restores the pre-block editing experience for posts, pages, and custom post "
"types, plus the classic Widgets screen. Front-end display of existing block "
"content is unaffected, and on a block theme the Site Editor stays available. "
"Off by default."
msgstr ""
"Restores the pre-block editing experience for posts, pages, and custom post "
"types, plus the classic Widgets screen. Front-end display of existing block "
"content is unaffected, and on a block theme the Site Editor stays available. "
"Off by default."

#: includes/strings.php:161
msgid "Upload Filenames"
msgstr "Upload Filenames"

#: includes/strings.php:162
msgid "Lowercase new upload filenames"
msgstr "Lowercase new upload filenames"

#: includes/strings.php:163
msgid ""
"Avoids case-sensitivity surprises when files move between case-insensitive "
"local/staging and case-sensitive Linux production. On by default; only "
"affects new uploads."
msgstr ""
"Avoids case-sensitivity surprises when files move between case-insensitive "
"local/staging and case-sensitive Linux production. On by default; only "
"affects new uploads."

#: includes/strings.php:166
msgid "Image Sizes"
msgstr "Image Sizes"

#: includes/strings.php:167
msgid "Show generated image sizes on attachments"
msgstr "Show generated image sizes on attachments"

#: includes/strings.php:168
msgid ""
"Adds a read-only panel to the attachment edit screen listing each generated "
"image size with its dimensions, file size, and URL — a quick way to confirm "
"what WordPress produced. On by default."
msgstr ""
"Adds a read-only panel to the attachment edit screen listing each generated "
"image size with its dimensions, file size, and URL — a quick way to confirm "
"what WordPress produced. On by default."

#: includes/strings.php:171
msgid "Email Deliverability"
msgstr "Email Deliverability"

#: includes/strings.php:172
msgid "Warn when site email looks broken"
msgstr "Warn when site email looks broken"

#: includes/strings.php:173
msgid ""
"Warns administrators when site email looks broken: a risky default From "
"address (invalid, or an example/local/test domain) on a non-local site, and "
"a bulk password reset that sent zero emails — replacing WordPress's "
"misleading \"success\" notice. On by default."
msgstr ""
"Warns administrators when site email looks broken: a risky default From "
"address (invalid, or an example/local/test domain) on a non-local site, and "
"a bulk password reset that sent zero emails — replacing WordPress's "
"misleading \"success\" notice. On by default."

#: includes/strings.php:177
msgid "Stop outgoing email unless this is the production site"
msgstr "Stop outgoing email unless this is the production site"

#: includes/strings.php:178
msgid ""
"A database copied from production brings real addresses and whatever mail "
"service production used. A cron run or a bulk action then emails real people "
"from a staging site or a laptop. Does nothing on production, so it cannot be "
"left on by mistake. Override per site with "
"<code>KEEL_ALLOW_NONPRODUCTION_MAIL</code> in <code>wp-config.php</code> or "
"the <code>keel_suppress_nonproduction_mail</code> filter."
msgstr ""
"A database copied from production brings real addresses and whatever mail "
"service production used. A cron run or a bulk action then emails real people "
"from a staging site or a laptop. Does nothing on production, so it cannot be "
"left on by mistake. Override per site with "
"<code>KEEL_ALLOW_NONPRODUCTION_MAIL</code> in <code>wp-config.php</code> or "
"the <code>keel_suppress_nonproduction_mail</code> filter."

#: includes/strings.php:181
msgid "Admin Search"
msgstr "Admin Search"

#: includes/strings.php:182
msgid "Search titles only in admin list tables"
msgstr "Search titles only in admin list tables"

#: includes/strings.php:183
msgid "Speeds up admin list-table search on big sites by matching titles only."
msgstr ""
"Speeds up admin list-table search on big sites by matching titles only."

#: includes/strings.php:186
msgid "Front-End Admin Bar"
msgstr "Front-End Admin Bar"

#: includes/strings.php:187
msgid ""
"The WordPress toolbar shown across the top of the site for logged-in users. "
"Hide it for non-admins or everyone, or auto-hide it so it slides out of the "
"way and returns on hover or keyboard focus (desktop only)."
msgstr ""
"The WordPress toolbar shown across the top of the site for logged-in users. "
"Hide it for non-admins or everyone, or auto-hide it so it slides out of the "
"way and returns on hover or keyboard focus (desktop only)."

#: includes/strings.php:189
msgid "Leave unchanged (WordPress default)"
msgstr "Leave unchanged (WordPress default)"

#: includes/strings.php:190
msgid "Hide for non-admins"
msgstr "Hide for non-admins"

#: includes/strings.php:191
msgid "Hide for everyone"
msgstr "Hide for everyone"

#: includes/strings.php:192
msgid "Auto-hide, reveal on hover or keyboard focus (desktop)"
msgstr "Auto-hide, reveal on hover or keyboard focus (desktop)"

#: includes/strings.php:196
msgid "Admin Menu Width"
msgstr "Admin Menu Width"

#: includes/strings.php:197
msgid ""
"Sets the width of the left admin menu, useful when plugin menu labels are "
"long. WordPress default is 160px. Leave unchanged and Keel sets no width at "
"all; choose 160px to assert core's width over a theme, host, or plugin that "
"has widened the menu."
msgstr ""
"Sets the width of the left admin menu, useful when plugin menu labels are "
"long. WordPress default is 160px. Leave unchanged and Keel sets no width at "
"all; choose 160px to assert core's width over a theme, host, or plugin that "
"has widened the menu."

#: includes/strings.php:198
msgid "Leave unchanged"
msgstr "Leave unchanged"

#: includes/strings.php:198
msgid "160px (WordPress default)"
msgstr "160px (WordPress default)"

#: includes/strings.php:198
msgid "200px"
msgstr "200px"

#: includes/strings.php:198
msgid "240px"
msgstr "240px"

#: includes/strings.php:198
msgid "280px"
msgstr "280px"

#: includes/strings.php:198
msgid "300px"
msgstr "300px"

#: includes/strings.php:201
msgid "Admin List Columns"
msgstr "Admin List Columns"

#: includes/strings.php:202
msgid "Add helper columns to admin list tables"
msgstr "Add helper columns to admin list tables"

#: includes/strings.php:203
msgid ""
"Adds at-a-glance columns to admin list tables: ID, featured image, and "
"modified date on posts and pages; file size on the Media library; "
"registration and last-login dates on Users. Last login is recorded from when "
"this is enabled onward. Off by default."
msgstr ""
"Adds at-a-glance columns to admin list tables: ID, featured image, and "
"modified date on posts and pages; file size on the Media library; "
"registration and last-login dates on Users. Last login is recorded from when "
"this is enabled onward. Off by default."

#: includes/strings.php:206
msgid "Environment Indicator"
msgstr "Environment Indicator"

#: includes/strings.php:207
msgid "Show the current environment in the admin bar"
msgstr "Show the current environment in the admin bar"

#: includes/strings.php:208
msgid ""
"Adds a color-coded label to the admin bar showing the current environment "
"(Production, Staging, Development, or Local) from "
"<code>wp_get_environment_type()</code> — a quick guard against acting on the "
"wrong site. Common local-development hosts are recognized automatically. Off "
"by default."
msgstr ""
"Adds a colour-coded label to the admin bar showing the current environment "
"(Production, Staging, Development, or Local) from "
"<code>wp_get_environment_type()</code> — a quick guard against acting on the "
"wrong site. Common local-development hosts are recognised automatically. Off "
"by default."

#: includes/strings.php:211
msgid "Remember Me"
msgstr "Remember Me"

#: includes/strings.php:212
msgid "Disable Remember Me and remove the login checkbox"
msgstr "Disable Remember Me and remove the login checkbox"

#: includes/strings.php:213
msgid ""
"Removes the Remember Me checkbox from the login form, so every login uses "
"the regular session length below. Useful for shared or kiosk machines."
msgstr ""
"Removes the Remember Me checkbox from the login form, so every login uses "
"the regular session length below. Useful for shared or kiosk machines."

#: includes/strings.php:216
msgid "Regular Session Length"
msgstr "Regular Session Length"

#: includes/strings.php:217 includes/strings.php:223
msgid "days"
msgstr "days"

#: includes/strings.php:218 includes/strings.php:224
msgid "day"
msgstr "day"

#: includes/strings.php:219
msgid ""
"How long a normal (non-remembered) login stays signed in. WordPress's "
"default is 2 days."
msgstr ""
"How long a normal (non-remembered) login stays signed in. WordPress's "
"default is 2 days."

#: includes/strings.php:222
msgid "Remember Me Length"
msgstr "Remember Me Length"

#: includes/strings.php:225
msgid ""
"How long a remembered login stays signed in. WordPress's default is 14 days. "
"It cannot be shorter than the regular session length above."
msgstr ""
"How long a remembered login stays signed in. WordPress's default is 14 days. "
"It cannot be shorter than the regular session length above."

#: includes/strings.php:228
msgid "Login Logo"
msgstr "Login Logo"

#: includes/strings.php:229
msgid ""
"The default logo links to wordpress.org, off your site. Left untouched by "
"default, since changing the login screen out of the box is intrusive. "
"Removing, unlinking, or replacing the logo always points the header link at "
"your home page. Replacing uses the logo set in the Customizer, or the site "
"icon if there is no logo; with neither set, the WordPress logo stays."
msgstr ""
"The default logo links to wordpress.org, off your site. Left untouched by "
"default, since changing the login screen out of the box is intrusive. "
"Removing, unlinking, or replacing the logo always points the header link at "
"your home page. Replacing uses the logo set in the Customizer, or the site "
"icon if there is no logo; with neither set, the WordPress logo stays."

#: includes/strings.php:231
msgid "Keep the WordPress logo and wordpress.org link (WordPress default)"
msgstr "Keep the WordPress logo and wordpress.org link (WordPress default)"

#: includes/strings.php:232
msgid "Remove the logo and the wordpress.org link"
msgstr "Remove the logo and the wordpress.org link"

#: includes/strings.php:233
msgid "Keep the logo, drop the wordpress.org link"
msgstr "Keep the logo, drop the wordpress.org link"

#: includes/strings.php:234
msgid "Replace the logo with your site logo"
msgstr "Replace the logo with your site logo"

#: includes/strings.php:238
msgid "Heartbeat API"
msgstr "Heartbeat API"

#: includes/strings.php:239
msgid "Slow background admin polling"
msgstr "Slow background admin polling"

#: includes/strings.php:240
msgid ""
"Slows admin polling to 60 seconds and drops it on the dashboard home. Off by "
"default: Heartbeat also powers autosave and post-lock warnings, so enabling "
"this will make them update less often."
msgstr ""
"Slows admin polling to 60 seconds and drops it on the dashboard home. Off by "
"default: Heartbeat also powers autosave and post-lock warnings, so enabling "
"this will make them update less often."

#: includes/strings.php:252
msgid "Security and Attack Surface"
msgstr "Security and Attack Surface"

#: includes/strings.php:253
msgid "Updates"
msgstr "Updates"

#: includes/strings.php:254
msgid "Content and Public Surfaces"
msgstr "Content and Public Surfaces"

#: includes/strings.php:255
msgid "Editor"
msgstr "Editor"

